menu "Companion Display Wi-Fi"
config COMPANION_DISPLAY_WIDTH
    int "Negotiated display width (px)"
    default 368
    help
        Physical panel width advertised in hello_ack and /api/status. The PC
        client scales, letterboxes and encodes to exactly this size, and the
        board's display module must accept frames of this width. Must match
        the board component's panel resolution.
config COMPANION_DISPLAY_HEIGHT
    int "Negotiated display height (px)"
    default 448
    help
        Physical panel height advertised in hello_ack and /api/status. See
        COMPANION_DISPLAY_WIDTH.
config COMPANION_HTTP_PORT
    int "HTTP and WebSocket port"
    default 80
config COMPANION_UDP_PORT
    int "UDP video port"
    default 5000
config COMPANION_AP_PASSWORD
    string "Provisioning AP password"
    default "companion-display"
config COMPANION_FRAME_TIMEOUT_MS
    int "Video frame idle timeout (ms)"
    range 2000 60000
    default 10000
    help
        After start_stream, if no complete video frame is received for this
        long the device ends the session, closes the control connection and
        returns to the main info screen. The PC client repeats a keepalive
        frame at 1 FPS for static content, so the default of 10 seconds only
        triggers when the stream is genuinely gone.
endmenu
